Requested subject: ${$json.subject}
Story context: ${$('Get Rams').first().json.Title}

Candidates (JSON array; use pageid to refer to them):
${JSON.stringify($json.candidates)}

Choose the single candidate that best shows the requested subject: the object itself, recognisable, and not a different model or a related object.

Reject any candidate where a person is the main subject (portrait, group, or someone using the object). Reject font diagrams, schematics, and illustrations unless the subject is the illustration itself.

Rate confidence:
- high: the title or description clearly identifies the requested subject and the model.
- medium: plausibly the subject but not confirmed by the metadata.
- low: unrelated, wrong model, person-led, or cannot tell.

If none match, return chosen_pageid null with confidence low.

Return ONLY JSON: {"chosen_pageid": 123 or null, "confidence": "high|medium|low", "reason": "one sentence"}` }}

